/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::addAnimationFABRIK(AnimationFABRIKOptions options, number order)
\brief Register a procedural pose modifier; requires an enabled animation pose.

See \ref procedural_fabrik_options.

Use setAnimationIKTarget(id, x, y, space) to update the scheduled target.
\param options Configuration described in the shared options reference.
\param order Ordering within the modifier stage; default zero.
\return Controller ID.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::addAnimationJiggle(AnimationJiggleOptions options, number order)
\brief Register a procedural pose modifier; requires an enabled animation pose.

See \ref procedural_jiggle_options and \ref procedural_jiggle_state.

\note Enable the animation pose and register the two-bone IK before decorating its target.
\par Example
\code{.js}
const ik = sprite.addAnimationIK({root: 'shoulder', middle: 'forearm',
    tip: 'hand', targetX: 15, targetY: 4});
const spring = sprite.addAnimationJiggle({mode: pdg.jiggleMode_IKTarget,
    ik, frequency: 3, dampingRatio: 0.35});
sprite.setAnimationIKTarget(ik, 8, 12);
// The desired target stays (8,12); the effective target moves toward it.
\endcode
\param options Configuration described in the shared options reference.
\param order Ordering within the modifier stage; default zero.
\return Controller ID.


\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly
\anchor procedural_jiggle_options
\par Jiggle configuration

All numbers are finite. Angles use radians, frequency uses Hz, and durations use seconds.
`mode` is required: `jiggleMode_Chain` rotates individual joints;
`jiggleMode_IKTarget` filters an existing two-bone IK target in world coordinates.
Chain entries are contiguous, ordered from root to tip. Sprite entries accept bone
names or IDs and include the root. Part entries are Parts from the same Sprite and
exclude the receiver. Independent Parts must have uniform, nonsingular scales;
dynamic Parts use target jiggle through setIKDriveTarget(), rather than chain jiggle.

| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mode` | Required | Chain or IK target mode. |
| `chain` | Empty | Chain entries; omit for IK target mode. |
| `ik` | 0 | Existing Sprite two-bone IK modifier ID; required for Sprite target mode. |
| `frequency` | 3 | Positive spring frequency, at most 60 Hz. |
| `dampingRatio` | 0.4 | Damping in [0,4]; below 1 oscillates, 1 is critical damping. |
| `influence` | 1 | Applied effect in [0,1]; zero keeps simulation running. |
| `inertia` | 0.5 | Chain response to pivot acceleration in [0,1]. |
| `length` | 0 | Positive lever length, or infer from authored length/next joint. Supply for a terminal Part. |
| `maxAngle` | pi/3 | Positive maximum chain deviation, at most pi. |
| `gravityX`, `gravityY` | 0 | World acceleration in engine units/second squared. |
| `maxAngularSpeed` | 20 | Positive chain speed cap in radians/second. |
| `maxDistance` | 32 | Positive target lag cap in world units. |
| `maxSpeed` | 1000 | Positive target speed cap in world units/second. |
| `maxStepSeconds` | 1/120 | Positive maximum simulation substep; at most 1/30 second. |
| `maxSubsteps` | 16 | Integer from 1 through 64. Longer steps reseed. |
| `teleportDistance` | 128 | Positive world displacement threshold for reseeding. |
| `teleportAngle` | pi/2 | Positive chain base-angle threshold, at most pi. |
| `enabled` | true | False bypasses the effect and freezes state; reenabling reseeds. |
| `resetOnSeek` | true | Sprite jiggle reseeds when the animation is explicitly sought. |
| `resetOnTeleport` | true | Reseed following large base/target changes. |
| `joints` | Empty | Sparse per-joint overrides in chain mode. |

Each joint override identifies a Sprite `bone` by name/ID or a Part by `part`
(or its stable `bone` ID returned by getJiggleOptions()). It may override `length`,
`frequency`, `dampingRatio`, `inertia`, `maxAngle`, `maxAngularSpeed`, `gravityX`
and `gravityY`. Omitted fields inherit controller tuning. Joint IDs must be unique
and belong to the chain. Settings patches replace the `joints` array as a whole.
Unknown settings and attempts to change topology through settings throw.

Modifiers execute by stage, then order, then registration. IK target jiggle runs
inside its associated solve; its registration order must be zero. Chain jiggle runs
in the post-constraint stage. Built-in controllers reject overlapping rotation
ownership. Custom pose callbacks may compose explicitly. Jiggle does not perform
obstacle queries: existing physical bodies and colliders handle contact in the
physics step, with physical IK drives receiving the filtered target.

\anchor procedural_fabrik_options
\par FABRIK configuration and results

Sprite `chain` contains at least three contiguous bone names/IDs; the last is the
endpoint. Part `chain` excludes the receiver and contains at least two descendants.
Solvers change rotating-joint angles and preserve link offsets, scale and endpoint
local orientation. Part FABRIK uses live setIKLimits() limits.

| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `targetX`, `targetY` | 0 | Sprite target; Part methods accept a Point separately. |
| `space` | Rig / Sprite | animationSpace_* for Sprite; partSpace_* for Part. |
| `influence` | 1 | Applied solve influence in [0,1]. |
| `tolerance` | 0.01 | Positive acceptable endpoint error in world units. |
| `maxIterations` | 16 | Integer from 1 through 256. |
| `bendDirection` | 1 | Exactly 1 or -1; deterministic initial bend direction. |
| `minimum`, `maximum` | Empty | Sprite local angle limits; one entry per rotating joint. |

`FABRIKResult` contains `solveError` (full solve), `reachError` (after influence),
`iterations`, `converged`, `reached`, `limited`, and `withinGeometricReach`.
Unreachable or constrained targets return a bounded best effort. `converged` refers
to full solve tolerance; `reached` refers to the applied endpoint. Invalid chains,
limits or nonfinite settings throw before modifying the pose.

\anchor procedural_jiggle_state
\par Jiggle results and state

`JiggleResult` contains `lagDistance`, applied `influence`, `simulatedSeconds`,
`substeps`, `limited`, and `reset`. Target mode additionally reports world-space
`desiredTarget`, `filteredTarget`, and `effectiveTarget` records with x/y fields.
Chain mode leaves target diagnostics at zero. Results describe the last evaluation.

`JiggleState` is an independent numerical snapshot: `version: 1`, `mode`, `chain`, associated `ik`, `rigRevision`, `initialized`,
`x`, `y`, `velocityX`, `velocityY`, and `joints`. Each joint contains world
`angle`, angular `velocity`, desired world heading `desired`, `pivotX`, `pivotY`,
`pivotVelocityX`, and `pivotVelocityY`. Restore only to the same mode and topology;
state restore does not replace settings, programmed base motion or fades.
Full Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve settings, fades and underlying Part rotations;
incremental updates transfer state while requiring unchanged controller topology.
Getters do not advance simulation. Springs use simulation time even while the clip
playback is paused, and simulation pause freezes them.
\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly
*/

