/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::removeAnimationJiggle(number id)
\brief Remove a jiggle controller.

See \ref procedural_jiggle_options and \ref procedural_jiggle_state.

\param id Controller ID returned by registration.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Part::solveFABRIK(Part[] chain, Point target, PartFABRIKOptions options)
\brief Solve or schedule a contiguous independent Part chain; chain excludes the receiver.

See \ref procedural_fabrik_options.

One-shot solve returns diagnostics and applies angles immediately.
Scheduled controller owners must be cleared before installing competing controllers.
\param chain Contiguous descendants, excluding this Part.
\param target Desired endpoint in the configured coordinate frame.
\param options Configuration described in the shared options reference.
\return An independent value describing the controller.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Part::setFABRIKTarget(Part[] chain, Point target, PartFABRIKOptions options)
\brief Solve or schedule a contiguous independent Part chain; chain excludes the receiver.

See \ref procedural_fabrik_options.

The last chain entry is the endpoint. Call again to update its target.
Use clearIKTarget() to remove the scheduled solver.
\param chain Contiguous descendants, excluding this Part.
\param target Desired endpoint in the configured coordinate frame.
\param options Configuration described in the shared options reference.
\return This Part for chaining.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Part::getFABRIKResult()
\brief Return the latest scheduled FABRIK diagnostics.

See \ref procedural_fabrik_options.

\return An independent value describing the controller.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Part::setJiggle(PartJiggleOptions options)
\brief Install chain jiggle or decorate an existing Part IK target.

See \ref procedural_jiggle_options and \ref procedural_jiggle_state.

\note Create a parent/child chain of independent Parts before installing chain jiggle.
\par Example
\code{.js}
root.setJiggle({mode: pdg.jiggleMode_Chain, chain: [middle, tip],
    length: 12, frequency: 2, dampingRatio: 0.3,
    joints: [{part: tip, frequency: 4}]});
root.kickJiggle({joint: middle, angularVelocity: 2});
// Angular velocity is in radians/second, rather than an angle offset.
\endcode
\param options Configuration described in the shared options reference.
\return This Part for chaining.
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Part::clearJiggle()
\brief Remove jiggle and restore the underlying programmed rotations.

See \ref procedural_jiggle_options and \ref procedural_jiggle_state.

\return This Part for chaining.
*/

